// Typechecks the extension against WXT's generated config, which supplies the
// #imports / browser types, the DOM lib the service worker and manager need, and
// the @core and @/ aliases that resolve into the shared app.
//
// It lives in this directory rather than at the repo root so an editor finds it.
// TypeScript picks a file's project by walking up from the file to the nearest
// tsconfig.json; with this at the root instead, everything under extension/
// belonged to no project, fell back to an inferred config with no path aliases,
// and every @core import read as a missing module in the editor while
// `npm run typecheck:extension` passed.
//
// WXT's defaults are realigned to the rest of the repo: it turns on
// noUncheckedIndexedAccess, which nothing else here uses, and leaves out the JSX
// setting its own Vite build applies. Needs `wxt prepare` to have generated .wxt/.
//
// `extends` only inherits compilerOptions, not `include` — a config that declares
// its own `include` drops the base's entirely. An imported file still enters the
// program through the module graph regardless, but an ambient file with no
// imports or exports, like src/vite-env.d.ts, only enters if `include` names it.
{
  "extends": "../.wxt/tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": false
  },
  "include": ["**/*", "../.wxt/wxt.d.ts", "../src/vite-env.d.ts"],
  "exclude": ["**/node_modules", "../.output"]
}
